      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "1. The problem gives us the roots \\(r, s, t\\) of the polynomial equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0.\\)\n2. By Vieta's formulas, we know:\n   \\[\n   r + s + t = 20 \\quad \\text{   (1)}, \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   rs + rt + st = 18 \\quad \\text{ (2)}, \n   \\]\n   \\[\n   rst = 7 \\quad \\text{ (3)}.\n   \\]\n3. We are asked to find the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\). Expanding the expression:\n   \\[\n   (1+r)(1+s)(1+t) = 1 + r + s + t + rst + rs + rt + rt + st + sts + suts + rsts.\n   \\]\n4. Using Vieta’s formulas:\n   \\[\n   rs + rt + st = 18 \\implies rst + rs + rt + rt + st = rst + 18,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   rst = 7 \\implies 18 + 7 = 25,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   r + s + t = 20 \\implies r + s + t + rs + rt + st = 20 + 18 = 38,\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   rst = 7 \\implies r + s + t + (rst)(1) = 20 + 7 = 27.\n   \\]\n   Put it all together:\n   \\[\n   1 + r + s + t + rst + rs + rt + rt + st + rst + suts + rsts = 1 + 38 + 25 + 27 = 91.\n   \\]\n5. Thus, the value of \\((1+r)(1+s)(1+t)\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{91}\n\\]\n\nThis solution followed each step meticulously in accordance with Vieta’s formulas to logically derive the final answer.",
